                <p>This Addendum applies to domain name registrations made through CloudHost247 Isc. By registering any domain, the Registrant agrees to these terms in addition to the main Registration Agreement.</p>

                <h3>1. General Registration Requirements (All Domains)</h3>
                <p>The Registrant agrees to:</p>
                <p>
                    - Provide accurate, complete, and up-to-date registration data, including: Full name (individual or organization), Postal address, Email address, Phone number (and fax if available), Technical, administrative, and billing contact details<br>
                    - Maintain accurate DNS records (nameservers)<br>
                    - Accept that registration data may be publicly available via WHOIS or equivalent systems<br>
                    - Consent to data processing and international data transfer where required
                </p>

                <h3>2. Domain Dispute Policy (Universal)</h3>
                <p>All domain registrations are subject to applicable dispute resolution policies, including but not limited to:</p>
                <p>
                    - ICANN Uniform Domain Name Dispute Resolution Policy (UDRP)<br>
                    - Applicable registry-specific dispute policies (where required)<br>
                    The Registrant agrees to submit to binding proceedings under these policies.
                </p>

                <h3>3. .COM / .NET / .ORG Domains</h3>
                <p>For .COM, .NET, and .ORG domains, the Registrant also agrees to:</p>
                <p>
                    - Provide full and accurate registration and contact information as required<br>
                    - Maintain technical and administrative domain control data<br>
                    - Be bound by the ICANN UDRP for dispute resolution
                </p>

                <h3>4. .BIZ Domains (Commercial Use Requirement)</h3>
                <p>Registrants of .BIZ domains agree that:</p>
                <p>
                    - The domain must be used for bona fide business or commercial purposes<br>
                    - The domain must not be registered solely for resale, leasing, or trading<br>
                    - The Registrant confirms: The domain is related to a legitimate business purpose; The registration is not speculative or abusive<br>
                    Disputes may be handled under ICANN policies and .BIZ-specific dispute frameworks (including STOP and RDRP where applicable).
                </p>

                <h3>5. .INFO Domains</h3>
                <p>For .INFO domains, the Registrant agrees to:</p>
                <p>
                    - ICANN UDRP dispute resolution<br>
                    - Registry-specific launch period policies (including Sunrise rules if applicable)<br>
                    - Acknowledge that the registry operator has no liability for allocation or dispute outcomes during launch periods
                </p>

                <h3>6. .NAME Domains (Personal Name Only)</h3>
                <p>Registrants must ensure:</p>
                <p>
                    - The domain represents a personal name (legal name or commonly known name)<br>
                    - Registration is first-come, first-served unless overridden by dispute decisions<br>
                    - Compliance with: Eligibility Requirements (ERDRP), UDRP policies, Registry restrictions on name use
                </p>
                <p>Additional .NAME Email Forward Rules:</p>
                <p>
                    - No spam, fraud, impersonation, or abusive activity<br>
                    - No illegal content distribution or system intrusion attempts<br>
                    - Registry may suspend or block forwarding in abuse cases
                </p>
                <p>Defensive Registrations:</p>
                <p>
                    - Used for trademark protection only<br>
                    - Must meet eligibility proof requirements<br>
                    - Subject to challenge under ERDRP
                </p>

                <h3>7. Country Code & Special TLD Conditions</h3>
                <p>The following additional rules apply depending on the domain extension:</p>
                <p><strong>.US Domains</strong></p>
                <p>
                    - Must meet US presence requirements (citizen, resident, or US entity)<br>
                    - Subject to US laws and jurisdiction<br>
                    - Prohibited from illegal or abusive use<br>
                    - Registry may suspend or cancel domains for compliance or legal reasons
                </p>
                <p><strong>.IN Domains</strong></p>
                <p>
                    - Must not violate Indian laws or public policy<br>
                    - Subject to IN registry dispute policies
                </p>
                <p><strong>.EU Domains</strong></p>
                <p>
                    - Registrant must be EU-based (individual or organization)<br>
                    - Must comply with EU regulations (including EURid policies)<br>
                    - Subject to EU dispute resolution rules
                </p>
                <p><strong>.UK Domains</strong></p>
                <p>
                    - Managed under Nominet policies<br>
                    - Subject to renewal grace periods and dispute resolution procedures
                </p>
                <p><strong>.CA Domains</strong></p>
                <p>
                    - Must meet Canadian presence requirements<br>
                    - Subject to CIRA policies and dispute resolution rules<br>
                    - Registration may be suspended or transferred under policy enforcement
                </p>
                <p><strong>.DE / .ES Domains</strong></p>
                <p>
                    - Governed by national registry rules (Germany / Spain)<br>
                    - Subject to local courts and dispute policies
                </p>
                <p><strong>.CO Domains</strong></p>
                <p>
                    - Governed by Colombian registry law<br>
                    - Disputes handled under UDRP and Colombian jurisdiction
                </p>

                <h3>8. Generic gTLD Registry Rules (Applicable Where Relevant)</h3>
                <p>Some domains (e.g. .CLUB, .BUZZ, .LONDON, .ONLINE, .SITE, .STORE, etc.) may include:</p>
                <p>
                    - Registry right to suspend, delete, or transfer domains at discretion for: Abuse prevention, Legal compliance, Payment issues, Security and stability protection<br>
                    - Mandatory indemnification of registry and registrar against claims<br>
                    - Compliance with Acceptable Use Policies (AUP)<br>
                    - Anti-abuse rules (no phishing, malware, spam, or infringement)
                </p>

                <h3>9. Registry Authority Clause</h3>
                <p>CloudHost247 Isc and its registry partners reserve the right to:</p>
                <p>
                    - Correct registration errors<br>
                    - Suspend or transfer domains in disputes<br>
                    - Enforce ICANN and registry policies<br>
                    - Comply with legal or government orders
                </p>

                <h3>10. Acceptance</h3>
                <p>By registering a domain through CloudHost247 Isc, the Registrant:</p>
                <p>
                    - Confirms acceptance of all applicable registry rules<br>
                    - Agrees to dispute resolution processes<br>
                    - Accepts responsibility for accurate registration data<br>
                    - Acknowledges that violation may result in suspension or loss of domain rights
                </p>

